H2900.definition:
or טוֹבִיָּהוּ; from H2896 (טוֹב) and H3050 (יָהּ); goodness of Jehovah;
Tobijah, the name of three Israelites and of one Samaritan
KJV: Tobiah, Tobijah.

H2901.definition:
a primitive root;
to spin
KJV: spin.

H2902.definition:
a primitive root;
to smear, especially with lime
KJV: daub, overlay, plaister, smut.

H2903.definition:
from an unused root meaning to go around or bind;
a fillet for the forehead
KJV: frontlet.

H2904.definition:
a primitive root;
to pitch over or reel; hence (transitively) to cast down or out
KJV: carry away, (utterly) cast (down, forth, out), send out.

H2905.definition:
from an unused root meaning to range in a regular manner;
a row; hence, a wall
KJV: row.

H2906.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6697 (צוּר);
a rock or hill
KJV: mountain.

H2907.definition:
a primitive root;
to pounce as a bird of prey
KJV: haste.

H2908.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H2901 (טָוָה);
hunger (as twisting)
KJV: fasting.

H2909.definition:
a primitive root;
to stretch a bow, as an archer
KJV: (bow-) shot.

H2910.definition:
from H2909 (טָחָה) (or H2902 (טוּחַ)) in the sense of overlaying;
(in the plural only) the kidneys (as being covered); hence (figuratively) the inmost thought
KJV: inward parts.

H2911.definition:
from H2912 (טָחַן);
a hand mill; hence, a millstone
KJV: to grind.

H2912.definition:
a primitive root;
to grind meal; hence, to be aconcubine (that being their employment)
KJV: grind(-er).

H2913.definition:
from H2912 (טָחַן);
a hand mill; hence (figuratively) chewing
KJV: grinding.

H2914.definition:
from an unused root meaning to burn;
a boil or ulcer (from the inflammation), especially a tumorin the anus or pudenda (the piles)
KJV: emerod.

H2915.definition:
from (the equiv. of) H2902 (טוּחַ);
mortar or plaster
KJV: daubing.

H2916.definition:
from an unused root meaning apparently to be sticky (rather perb. a demonstrative); from H2894 (טוּא), through the idea of dirt to be swept away);
mud or clay; figuratively, calamity
KJV: clay, dirt, mire.

H2917.definition:
(Aramaic) perhaps, by interchange, for a word corresponding to H2916 (טִיט);
clay
KJV: miry.

H2918.definition:
feminine of (an equivalent to) H2905 (טוּר);
a wall; hence, a fortress or a hamlet
KJV: (goodly) castle, habitation, palace, row.

H2919.definition:
from H2926 (טָלַל);
dew (as covering vegetation)
KJV: dew.

H2920.definition:
(Aramaic) the same as H2919 (טַל)
{dew (as covering vegetation)}
KJV: dew.

H2921.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to cover with pieces; i.e. (by implication) to spot or variegate (as tapestry)
KJV: clouted, with divers colours, spotted.

H2923.definition:
from the plural of H2922 (טְלָא); lambs;
Telaim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Telaim.

H2924.definition:
by variation for H2922 (טְלָא);
a lamb
KJV: lamb.

H2925.definition:
from H2904 (טוּל);
overthrow or rejection
KJV: captivity.

H2926.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to strew over, i.e. (by implication) to cover in or plate (with beams)
KJV: cover.

H2927.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2926 (טָלַל);
to cover with shade
KJV: have a shadow.

H2928.definition:
from an unused root meaning to break up or treat violently; oppression;
Telem, the name of a place in Idumaea, also of a temple doorkeeper
KJV: Telem.

H2929.definition:
from the same as H2728 (חָרְגֹּל); oppressive;
Talmon, a temple doorkeeper
KJV: Talmon.

H2930.definition:
a primitive root;
to be foul, especially in a ceremial or moral sense (contaminated)
KJV: defile (self), pollute (self), be (make, make self, pronounce) unclean, [idiom] utterly.

H2931.definition:
from H2930 (טָמֵא);
foul in a religious sense
KJV: defiled, [phrase] infamous, polluted(-tion), unclean.

H2932.definition:
from H2930 (טָמֵא);
religious impurity
KJV: filthiness, unclean(-ness).

H2933.definition:
a collateral form of H2930 (טָמֵא);
to be impure in a religious sense
KJV: be defiled, be reputed vile.

H2934.definition:
a primitive root;
to hide (by covering over)
KJV: hide, lay privily, in secret.

H2935.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to weave;
a basket (of interlaced osiers)
KJV: basket.

H2936.definition:
a primitive root;
to soil
KJV: defile.

H2937.definition:
a primitive root;
to wander; causatively to lead astray
KJV: seduce.

H2938.definition:
a primitive root;
to taste; figuratively, to perceive
KJV: [idiom] but, perceive, taste.

H2939.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2938 (טָעַם);
to taste; causatively to feed
KJV: make to eat, feed.

H2940.definition:
from H2938 (טָעַם);
properly, a taste, i.e. (figuratively) perception; by implication, intelligence; transitively, a mandate
KJV: advice, behaviour, decree, discretion, judgment, reason, taste, understanding.

H2942.definition:
(Aramaic) from H2939 (טְעַם), and equivalent to H2941 (טַעַם);
properly, flavor; figuratively, judgment (both subjective and objective); hence, account (both subjectively and objectively)
KJV: [phrase] chancellor, [phrase] command, commandment, decree, [phrase] regard, taste, wisdom.

H2943.definition:
a primitive root;
to load a beast
KJV: lade.

H2944.definition:
a primitive root;
to stab
KJV: thrust through.

H2945.definition:
from H2952 (טָפַף) (perhaps referring to the tripping gait of children);
a family (mostly used collectively in the singular)
KJV: (little) children (ones), families.

H2946.definition:
a primitive root; or perhaps a denominative from H2947 (טֵפַח), from dandling on the palms
to flatten out or extend (as a tent); figuratively, to nurse achild (as promotive of growth);
KJV: span, swaddle.

H2947.definition:
from H2946 (טָפַח);
a spread of the hand, i.e. a palm-breadth (not 'span' of the fingers); architecturally, a corbel (as a supporting palm)
KJV: coping, hand-breadth.

H2948.definition:
from H2946 (טָפַח) (the same as H2947 (טֵפַח))
{a spread of the hand, i.e. a palm-breadth (not 'span' of the fingers); architecturally, a corbel (as a supporting palm)}
KJV: hand-breadth (broad).

H2949.definition:
from H2946 (טָפַח);
nursing
KJV: span long.

H2950.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to stick on as apatch; figuratively, to impute falsely
KJV: forge(-r), sew up.

H2951.definition:
of foreign derivation;
a military governor
KJV: captain.

H2953.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H6852 (צָפַר), and meaning the same as H6856 (צִפֹּרֶן);
a finger-nail; also a hoof or claw
KJV: nail.

H2954.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, apparently to be thick; figuratively, to be stupid
KJV: be fat.

H2955.definition:
probably from H5197 (נָטַף); a dropping (of ointment);
Taphath, an Israelitess
KJV: Taphath.

H2956.definition:
a primitive root;
to drive on; figuratively, to follow close
KJV: continual.

H2957.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2956 (טָרַד);
to expel
KJV: drive.

H2958.definition:
a variation of H2962 (טֶרֶם);
not yet
KJV: before.

H2959.definition:
a primitive root;
to overburden
KJV: weary.

H2960.definition:
from H2959 (טָרַח);
a burden
KJV: cumbrance, trouble.

H2961.definition:
from an unused root apparently meaning to be moist;
properly, dripping; hence, fresh (i.e. recently made such)
KJV: new, putrefying.

H2962.definition:
from an unused root apparently meaning to interrupt or suspend;
properly, non-occurrence; used adverbially, not yet or before
KJV: before, ere, not yet.

H2963.definition:
a primitive root;
to pluck off or pull to pieces; causatively to supply with food (as in morsels)
KJV: catch, [idiom] without doubt, feed, ravin, rend in pieces, [idiom] surely, tear (in pieces).

H2964.definition:
from H2963 (טָרַף);
something torn, i.e. a fragment, e.g. a fresh leaf, prey, food
KJV: leaf, meat, prey, spoil.

H2965.definition:
from H2963 (טָרַף);
recently torn off, i.e. fresh
KJV: pluckt off.

H2966.definition:
feminine (collectively) of H2964 (טֶרֶף);
prey, i.e. flocks devoured by animals
KJV: ravin, (that which was) torn (of beasts, in pieces).

H2967.definition:
(Aramaic) from a name of foreign derivation;
a Tarpelite (collectively) or inhabitants of Tarpel, a place in Assyria
KJV: Tarpelites. y

H2968.definition:
a primitive root;
to desire
KJV: long.

H2969.definition:
a primitive root;
to be suitable
KJV: appertain.

H2970.definition:
or יַאֲזַנְיָהוּ; from H238 (אָזַן) and H3050 (יָהּ); heard of Jah;
Jaazanjah, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Jaazaniah. Compare H3153 (יְזַנְיָה).

H2971.definition:
from H215 (אוֹר); enlightener;
Jair, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Jair.

H2972.definition:
patronymically from H2971 (יָאִיר);
a Jairite or descendant of Jair
KJV: Jairite.

H2973.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to be slack, i.e. (figuratively) to be foolish
KJV: dote, be (become, do) foolish(-ly).

H2974.definition:
a primitive root (probably rather the same as H2973 (יָאַל) through the idea of mental weakness);
properly, to yield, especially assent; hence (pos.) to undertake as an act of volition
KJV: assay, begin, be content, please, take upon, [idiom] willingly, would.

H2975.definition:
of Egyptian origin;
a channel, e.g. a fosse, canal, shaft; specifically the Nile, as the one river of Egypt, including its collateral trenches; also the Tigris, as the main river of Assyria
KJV: brook, flood, river, stream.

H2976.definition:
a primitive root;
to desist, i.e. (figuratively) to despond
KJV: (cause to) despair, one that is desperate, be no hope.

H2977.definition:
or יֹאשִׁיָּהוּ; from the same root as H803 (אֲשׁוּיָה) and H3050 (יָהּ); founded of Jah;
Joshijah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Josiah.

H2978.definition:
from H857 (אָתָה);
an entry
KJV: entrance.

H2979.definition:
from the same as H871 (אֲתָרִים); stepping;
Jeatherai, an Israelite
KJV: Jeaterai.

H2980.definition:
a primitive root;
to bawl
KJV: cry out.

H2981.definition:
from H2986 (יָבַל);
produce, i.e. a crop or (figuratively) wealth
KJV: fruit, increase.

H2982.definition:
from H947 (בּוּס); trodden, i.e. threshing-place;
Jebus, the original name of Jerusalem
KJV: Jebus.

H2983.definition:
patrial from H2982 (יְבוּס);
a Jebusite or inhabitant of Jebus
KJV: Jebusite(-s).

H2984.definition:
from H977 (בָּחַר); choice;
Jibchar, an Israelite
KJV: Ibhar.

H2985.definition:
from H995 (בִּין); intelligent;
Jabin, the name of two Canaanitish kings
KJV: Jabin.

H2986.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to flow; causatively, to bring (especially with pomp)
KJV: bring (forth), carry, lead (forth).

H2987.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2986 (יָבַל);
to bring
KJV: bring, carry.

H2988.definition:
from H2986 (יָבַל);
a stream
KJV: (water-) course, stream.

H2989.definition:
the same as H2988 (יָבָל);
Jabal, an antediluvian
KJV: Jabal.

H2990.definition:
from H2986 (יָבַל);
having running sores
KJV: wen.

H2991.definition:
from H1104 (בָּלַע) and H5971 (עַם); devouring people;
Jibleam, a place in Palestine
KJV: Ibleam.

H2992.definition:
a primitive root of doubtful meaning; used only as a denominative from H2993 (יָבָם);
to marry a (deceased) brother's widow
KJV: perform the duty of a husband's brother, marry.

H2993.definition:
from (the orig. of) H2992 (יָבַם);
a brotherin-law
KJV: husband's brother.

H2994.definition:
feminine participle of H2992 (יָבַם);
a sister-in-law
KJV: brother's wife, sister in law.

H2995.definition:
from H1129 (בָּנָה) and H410 (אֵל); built of God;
Jabneel, the name of two places in Palestine
KJV: Jabneel.

H2996.definition:
from H1129 (בָּנָה); a building;
Jabneh, a place in Palestine
KJV: Jabneh.

H2997.definition:
from H1129 (בָּנָה) and H3050 (יָהּ); built of Jah;
Jibnejah, an Israelite
KJV: Ibneiah.

H2998.definition:
from H1129 (בָּנָה) and H3050 (יָהּ); building of Jah;
Jibnijah, an Israelite
KJV: Ibnijah.

H2999.definition:
probably from H1238 (בָּקַק); pouring forth;
Jabbok, a river east of the Jordan
KJV: Jabbok.
